  "result": "The rule and its four witnesses for NRS_484B_220_2 passed the gate with **OK** on the first run, so only 1 of the 6 runs was used.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_220_2.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a road user that is a vehicle under the definition `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies some roundabout region.\n- **The duty:** for every roundabout the subject occupies, it must not be circulating clockwise about it (`drv_motion_circulating_clockwise_about`). The two tolerances come from the node's parameters `p.halt_speed_tolerance` and `p.roundabout_clockwise_sin_tol`.\n- The duty repeats the full \"roundabout the subject occupies\" selection rather than sharing a variable name with the applicability, as required.\n- I didn't need to make any reading choices beyond the node's own, so `narrowings` is empty.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_220_2.lean`) use one roundabout, a 60 m square with its centre at (0,0), and a motor vehicle at 6 m/s:\n\n| Witness | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | 15 m south of the centre, heading west, so going clockwise | violated |\n| permit | same spot, heading east, so going counter-clockwise | compliant |\n| idle | on a straight roadway 160 m away from the roundabout | not applicable |\n| blind | as forbid, but the vehicle's velocity is not observed | unknown |\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
